   {
    "model_version": "gemini-3.7-flash",
    "content": {
     "parts": [
      {
       "text": "The latest pipeline run (**vertex-demo-e2e-4-20261126**, data as of 2026-11-26) succeeded across all steps, producing customer churn scores with feature explanations, 180-day CLV predictions, and 30-day category demand forecasts.\n\n### Model Quality Summary:\n* **Churn (AutoML Tabular):** AUC-PR for the reorders class is **0.227** against a test positive rate of **6.9%** (AUC-ROC: 0.761). It demonstrates meaningful signal over baseline reorder rates, though precision remains modest (25.3% at threshold 0.155).\n* **CLV (Custom XGBoost):** RMSE is **$43.11** versus a baseline RMSE of **$43.93**, with an **$R^2$ of 0.037**. The model barely beats a simple baseline average and explains very little spend variance; use it cautiously for rough decile ranking rather than exact dollar forecasts.\n* **Demand (BigQuery ML ARIMA_PLUS):** Average holdout MAPE across 26 categories is **39.2%**, and the 90% prediction band coverage is only **49.6%** (well below the target 90%). The forecast bands are far too narrow, meaning real-world demand frequently falls outside the expected range.",
